<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Betting on the Big Game</strong></p>
<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;">According to <a href="https://sportsbook.draftkings.com/teams/football/nfl/san-francisco-49ers--odds" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DraftKings, the 49ers</a> are currently favored by 2 points over the Chiefs. With the moneyline standing at -125 for the 49ers and +105 for the Chiefs, sports enthusiasts are eagerly awaiting the outcome of this highly anticipated matchup.</p>
<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;"><strong>Fanfare and Festivities: Super Bowl Consumer Spending</strong></p>
<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;">The latest data from <a href="https://nrf.com/super-bowl-data-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NRF and Prosper Insights & Analytics</a> reveals that a staggering 200.5 million U.S. adults plan to tune in to the Super Bowl, with total spending expected to reach a record-breaking $17.3 billion. From food and beverages to apparel and decorations, Americans are pulling out all the stops to make this year’s Super Bowl festivities truly unforgettable.</p>
